  "text_md": "CERN/DG/RB 2002-338 Page 10\n\nEXPLORER. It had been interrupted because of the higher priority of the LHC cost overrun discussions. The Research Board agreed to restart this procedure starting with L3+C at the next Research Board.\n\nThe next meeting of the Research Board will take place on\n\n## Thursday, 12 September 2002.\n\nENCLOSURES th [1]Minutes of the 12 INTC meeting held on 13 May 2002 (INTC 2002-026/INTC 12) th [2]Minutes of the 58 LHCC meeting held on 15-16 May 2002 (LHCC 2002-019/LHCC 58) th [3]Minutes of the 58 SPSC meeting held on 21 May 2002 (SPSC 2002-022/SPSC 58)\n\n## REFERENCES\n\nth [ 1]Minutes of the 157 meeting of the Research Board held on 11 March 2002 (CERN/DG/RB 2001-332, M157) th [ 2]Minutes of the 158 meeting of the Research Board held on 11 April 2002 (CERN/DG/RB 2001-335, M158) [ 3]Neutron Cross Sections for the Pb Isotopes Implications for ADS and Nucleosynthesis (INTC 2001-020/P142) [ 4]Measurements of fission cross sections for the isotopes relevant to the Thorium fuel cycle (INTC 2001-025/P145) 232 231 234 236 [ 5]Measurement of the neutron capture cross sections of Th, Pa, U and U; (INTC 2002-013/P154) [ 6]An Energy Upgrade of REX-Isolde to 3.1 MeV/u and Acceleration of Heavier Masses up to A=150 (INTC 2002-009/P152) [ 7]Fusion Reactions at the Coulomb Barrier with Neutron-rich Mg Isotopes (INTC 2002- 014/P155) [ 8]Evolution of single particle and collective properties in the neutron-rich Mg isotopes (INTC 2002-020/P159) [ 9]Summary, plan and resources of RD39 projects (LHCC 2002-015, Status Report/ RD39 1) [10]Development of radiation hard semiconductor devices for very high luminosity colliders (LHCC 2002-003/P6) [11]Status Report on the NA60 Pixel Detector Project (SPSC 2002-024/M689) [12]Status Report of the HARP experiment (SPSC 2002-019/M685) [13]Future plans; The DIRAC Collaboration (SPSC 2002-018/M684)\n",
